      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In view of the remarkable number of cases of gnathogenous headache it is advisable to submit headache patients to a thorough dental and radiological inspection, even in cases of anodontous jaws, in order to identify unerupted teeth. Such an examination with consequent dental or surgical thrapy can in many cases spare lengthy neurological diagnostic or therapeutic procedures, possibly in hospital."},
